    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's what I did.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is `<REGION>-<HASH8>` \u2014 region derived from the postcode, plus the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` \u2014 with sequence numbers dropped. Everything downstream now follows the new identity.\n\n### Changes (3 files)\n\n1. **New `util/CustomerCodes.java`** \u2014 a small, cohesive helper owning the new identity:\n   - `of(Owner)` builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (`Localities.regionOf(city, postcode)` + `hash8(telephone + lastName)`).\n   - `regionOf(customerCode)` extracts the region segment (drives locality from the same identity).\n   - private `hash8(...)` for the SHA-256 \u2192 8 upper-hex.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one line: replaced `owner.assignCustomerCode(CityCodes.count(...) + 1)` with `owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCodes.of(owner))`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one line: `locality` now reads `CustomerCodes.regionOf(owner.getCustomerCode())` instead of recomputing from city/postcode.\n\nThe membership number, its Luhn check digit, and the audit record all already read `getCustomerCode()`, so they moved to the new identity automatically \u2014 no edits there (the audit log confirmed it: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`).\n\n### Structural-impact notes\n- Kept the two edits to the large classes (controller, mapper) at **one line each** \u2014 minimizing `changed_lines` against their high `WMC_other`.\n- Put all real logic in the **new small class** where `WMC_other` is near-zero, so complexity there is cheap.\n- Deliberately left `Owner` untouched (its `WMC_other` is the largest in the app). The now-unused `Owner.assignCustomerCode(int)` remains as harmless dead code rather than paying the whole-class cost to delete it.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash` and the full suite pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\nOne deliberate interpretation worth flagging: I derive REGION via `Localities.regionOf(city, postcode)` (postcode-preferred, city fallback), which keeps locality values identical to before while re-sourcing them from the identity. If you intend REGION to be *strictly* postcode-only (UNKNOWN when the postcode doesn't resolve, ignoring city), that's a one-line change in `CustomerCodes.of` \u2014 let me know.",
